sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Browser
    participant Next as Next.js<br/>(Server Actions / RSC)
    participant Express as Express<br/>(/bookings, /webhooks/stripe)
    participant Stripe
    participant DB as Postgres
    participant Resend

    rect rgb(235, 245, 255)
    Note over Browser,DB: 1. Reserve dates and start payment (POST /bookings)
    Browser->>Next: submit booking form -> submitBooking() Server Action
    Next->>Express: POST /bookings<br/>Cookie forwarded (userId from session, never client-supplied)
    Express->>DB: INSERT booking status='pending'<br/>(EXCLUDE constraint reserves the dates)
    alt overlapping dates, hold > 15 min old
        Express->>DB: DELETE the stale pending row, retry the insert
    else overlapping dates, still within hold
        Express-->>Next: 409 Conflict
        Next-->>Browser: show "dates no longer available"
    end
    Express->>Stripe: paymentIntents.create<br/>(amount, currency, metadata.bookingId)
    Stripe-->>Express: PaymentIntent { id, client_secret }
    Express->>DB: UPDATE booking SET stripePaymentIntentId
    Express-->>Next: 201 { booking, clientSecret }
    Next-->>Browser: render PaymentStep (mounts Stripe Elements)
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 235)
    Note over Browser,Stripe: 2. Confirm payment - entirely client-side (ADR-0011)
    Browser->>Browser: Guest enters card into CardElement
    Browser->>Stripe: stripe.confirmCardPayment(clientSecret, { card })
    Note right of Stripe: Express/Next are never in this call -<br/>card details never touch our servers
    alt card declined
        Stripe-->>Browser: error - Guest can retry, same PaymentIntent
    else payment succeeds
        Stripe-->>Browser: success
        Browser->>Browser: router.push(/bookings/:id)<br/>(client-side nav, no Stripe return_url)
    end
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
    Note over Stripe,Resend: 3. Stripe confirms asynchronously via webhook
    Stripe->>Express: POST /webhooks/stripe (payment_intent.succeeded)<br/>raw body, signed
    Express->>Express: verifyWebhookSignature(payload, stripe-signature)
    Express->>DB: SELECT booking by PaymentIntent.metadata.bookingId
    alt booking not found (hold already reclaimed)
        Express->>Stripe: refund(paymentIntentId)
    else already confirmed (redelivery)
        Express-->>Stripe: 200 (no-op)
    else booking still pending
        Express->>Stripe: retrieve PaymentIntent (expand payment_method)
        Stripe-->>Express: card last4
        Express->>DB: UPDATE booking SET status='confirmed', cardLast4<br/>WHERE status='pending'
        Express->>Resend: send booking confirmation email<br/>(idempotencyKey: booking-confirmation/:id)
    end
    Express-->>Stripe: 200 OK
    end

    rect rgb(250, 240, 255)
    Note over Browser,DB: 4. Confirmation page catches up to the webhook
    Browser->>Next: GET /bookings/:id
    Next->>Express: GET /bookings/:id
    Express->>DB: SELECT booking
    DB-->>Express: status still 'pending' (webhook may lag)
    Express-->>Next: booking
    Next-->>Browser: render "confirming payment" + mount PendingBookingWatcher
    loop every 3s, up to ~60s
        Browser->>Next: checkBookingStatus() Server Action
        Next->>Express: GET /bookings/:id
        Express->>DB: SELECT booking
        DB-->>Express: status
        Express-->>Next: status
        Next-->>Browser: status
    end
    Browser->>Browser: status='confirmed' -> router.refresh()<br/>re-renders the confirmed view
    end
